  "note": "Urban district election, 15 January 1932. There was no contest: the twelve outgoing members were the only nominations and were returned unopposed (Northern Whig and Belfast Post, 6 January 1932, p. 3). The report says simply that the outgoing twelve were nominated and no other candidates came forward; no party labels or votes were printed. Returned unopposed."
